Package Management

Ubuntu uses the APT package manager.

Update Package List
sudo apt update

Purpose:

Refreshes the package list from software repositories.

It checks for available software updates but does not install them.

Upgrade Installed Packages
sudo apt upgrade

Purpose:

Installs available updates for software already installed on the system.

Install Package
sudo apt install tree

Purpose:

Installs new software.

Remove Package
sudo apt remove tree

Purpose:

Removes installed software from the system.
